## Method
RUN = `git -C /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2 archive d9bf7ef` (everything WS
ships). BASE = `git archive 643fa54` (pre-WS). Built with
`nice -n 19 go build` (GOMAXPROCS=4) into a scratch dir, each against its own
`cp -rL` of the real data/ directory, isolated ports 18080/18081 (never
:8080), one server up at a time while Playwright drove it, killed after each
phase; `ss -ltnp | grep budget2` at the end shows only the pre-existing
:8080 (pid 1836774) — never contacted. axe-core 4.13.0
(/home/darrell/.npm/_npx/e003b6b07d062486/node_modules/axe-core, matching
the globally-installed @axe-core/cli 4.13.0 earlier WS checkers used)
injected into the live Chromium page via Playwright, not hand-built HTML.
Scope confirmed via a byte-level `filecmp` directory diff (not the
rtk-rewritten `diff`/`git diff`): WS touches only internal/handlers/whatif,
internal/services/retirement (non-rendering engine code),
internal/templates/render.go, four web/static/js files, and the
web/templates/components/whatif/* + pages/whatif.html templates. Every
other page is byte-identical to BASE.

